  "period_note": "Solo basis. This report's own 'Five Years Performance' table is badly corrupted (its FY2017 column appears to duplicate stale FY2013 figures from elsewhere in the OCR'd/scanned pages of this archive copy) and was NOT used. Instead, FY2017's own contemporaneous Statement of Financial Position and Statement of Comprehensive Income (Solo, headed simply 'Statement of Financial Position' - distinguished in this same report from its separate 'Consolidated Statement of Financial Position' for the Group) were used for balance-sheet and core P&L figures, cross-checked against the FY2019 and FY2021 annual reports' 'Five Years Performance' tables (both show FY2017 as a comparative column and agree with each other and with the own-report figures for every item checked, including the capital-adequacy figures which are NOT in FY2017's own primary financial statements). Provision shortfall (loans+OBS): required 25,749,800,997 Taka vs. maintained 13,199,226,136 Taka, a shortfall of 12,550,574,861 Taka (BDT 1,255.06 crore), again BB-forborne per the bank's own note. Net interest income per FY2017's own Solo P&L (351.24 crore) differs slightly (~1%) from the figure reproduced in later reports' comparative tables (354.59, used here for consistency with the rest of the row); operating profit reconciles to within 0.08 crore either way. Separately, even within the five-year table itself, Interest income (1,684.22) minus Interest expenses (1,329.01) = 355.21, a residual 0.62 crore (0.17%) above the table's own printed Net interest income (354.59) - an immaterial rounding residual (each cell appears independently rounded to 2 decimals in the source) rather than a substantive error; flagged per the dataset's 0.05% threshold for completeness.",
